<title>POLAND: Polish industrial output down 3.4 pct in January.</title>
<headline>Polish industrial output down 3.4 pct in January.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-02-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Poland's industrial output (unadjusted) fell 3.4 percent in January, after a 2.1 percent rise in December, and was 8.6 percent higher than in January 1996, the Central Statistical Office (GUS) said.  </p>
<p> POLISH INDUSTRIAL OUTPUT     JANUARY   DECEMBER    JAN 1996</p>
<p> month/month change (pct)	-3.4	  2.1	  -2.6</p>
<p> yr/yr change (pct)		 8.6	 10.1	   9.5</p>
<p> index (mthly avge 1994=100)  123.4	125.9	   N/A</p>
<p> mining m/m change		  7.5	 -0.5	   4.8</p>
<p> mining yr/yr change	     -0.8	 -2.2	   4.2</p>
<p> manufacturing m/m change	-4.8	  0.7	  -3.1</p>
<p> manufacturing yr/yr change    10.7	 13.3	  12.1</p>
<p> utilities m/m change	    -0.7	 15.9	  -4.8</p>
<p> utilities yr/yr change	   2.8	 -1.8	  -1.2 @</p>
<p>NOTES - January 1996 and 1997 had 23 working days and December 1996 had 21 working days.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
